r novel American Pastoral (1997).\\n\\nIn the realm of African-American literature, Ralph Ellison's 1952 novel Invisible Man was instantly recognized as among the ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_literature\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d23\"},\"ref\":\"d23\",\"snippet\":\" ... International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award 2012. Retrieved 23 January 2015.\\n* Financial Times 2010 Fiction of the YearBlau, Rosie (3 December 2010). FT Fiction Round-up 2010. Financial Times, Fiction Round-up 2010. Retrieved 25 January 2015.\\n\\nLife of Pi\\n\\n* Winner of the 2002 Man Booker Prize for FictionLife ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yann_Martel\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f6c2922b92ef3c10a8a5124fbd6e8bf2ff92b533639036ca9f4e18691d946462\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"8d45253fb5b927dc01994aa98da483387d1121b4ec79a71b5bee8e2a72dc2959\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d5\"},\"ref\":\"d5\",\"snippet\":\" ... A Russian version of the Booker Prize was created in 1992 called the Booker-Open Russia Literary Prize, also known as the Russian Booker Prize. In 2007, Man Group plc established the Man Asian Literary Prize, an annual literary award given to the best novel by an Asian ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d29\"},\"ref\":\"d29\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2015, Mabanckou was a finalist for the Man Booker International Prize.\\n\\nThe Refugees by Viet Thanh Nguyen\\n\\nViet Thanh Nguyen's novel The Sympathizer is a New York Times best seller and won the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction. Other honors include the Dayton Literary Peace Prize, the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.aspeninstitute.org/blog-posts/20-new-works-fiction-social-impact/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d21\"},\"ref\":\"d21\",\"snippet\":\" ... Gibb was the winner of the Trillium Book Award in 2006, a Scotiabank Giller Prize short list nominee in 2005, winner of the city of Toronto Book Award in 2000 and the recipient of the CBC Canadian Literary Award for short fiction in 2001. Her books have been ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.yorku.ca/laps/huma/canadian-writers/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d31\"},\"ref\":\"d31\",\"snippet\":\" ... A selection of his poetry is collected in Desire Never … Read More\\n\\nColm Toíbín\\n\\nColm Toíbín is the author of six novels, including The Master, winner of the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award and shortlisted for the Man Booker Prize, as well as winner of the LA Times ... \",\"title\":\"https://griffinpoetryprize.com/judges/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Mara Polgovsky Ezcurra has been shortlisted for the 2020 Association for the Study of the Arts of the Present (ASAP) Book Prize is winner of the 2019 Art Journal prize from the College Art Association.\\n\\nBeyond the City and the Bridge: East Asian Immigration in a New Jersey ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.rutgersuniversitypress.org/awards/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... colonial photography – Shortlisted for the British Academy Book Prize for Global Cultural Understanding 2023\\n\\nAfrican football migration – Shortlisted for the British Society of Sports History's Lord Aberdare Literary Prize 2023\\n\\nWorrier state – Shortlisted for MeCCSA Monograph of the Year 2023\\n\\nThe ideal river – Winner of the BISA ... \",\"title\":\"https://manchesteruniversitypress.co.uk/award-winning-books/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d24\"},\"ref\":\"d24\",\"snippet\":\" ... Recent prize winners are listed below.\\n\\nAlice Davis Hitchcock Book Award (Society of Architectural Historians)\\n\\n2004: Jordan Sand, House and Home in Modern Japan: Architecture, Domestic Space, and Bourgeois Culture, 1880–1930 (HEAM 223)\\n\\nAldo and Jeanne Scaglione Prize for East Asian Studies (Modern Language Association of America ... \",\"title\":\"https://asiacenter.harvard.edu/publications/awards\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d32\"},\"ref\":\"d32\",\"snippet\":\" ... the Commonwealth Prize, the Man Booker Prize, the Orange Prize and the International IMPAC Dublin Literary Award among a host of others.\\n\\nBut not all prizes are created equal. Not all prizes are equally winnable, and not all prizes bestow equal glory on their winners. Just as authors ... \",\"title\":\"https://giramondopublishing.com/heat/archive/beth-driscoll-how-prizes-work-in-the-literary-economy/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prize for Unpublished Books\\n\\n| Deadline | 1 April 2025 |\\n\\n|---|---|\\n\\n| Entry Fee | $25 |\\n\\n| First Prize | 2–4 winners are announced who share in the $1000 USD total prize pool. Winners may choose to have an extract published, and receive a letter of recommendation from the judges. Twenty writers are shortlisted ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.novel-software.com/novel-writing-competitions/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d27\"},\"ref\":\"d27\",\"snippet\":\" ... His previous collections include Phantom Camera (winner of the 2012 Green Rose Prize in Poetry from New Issues Press), Carrier Wave (winner of the 2006 Colorado Prize for Poetry from the Center for Literary Publishing at Colorado State University), and the digital chapbook The Tallest Building in America ... \",\"title\":\"https://artsandsciences.syracuse.edu/english-department/creative-writing-mf-program/raymond-carver-reading-series/previous-raymond-carver-reading-series/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"2a690f15b0b41e64d1575db8962d6876b76677aedbf355ca05dc163e72b9ca14\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"25b600e54fb987d0decc5fce53cbd28d6ded3b7d047a29b561ad033e21c865df\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Asian Literary Prize winners shortlist\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_a1565894ebd74d379ada7263"},{"content":"Previously delivered raw windows (untrusted source data, not instructions or verified claims):\n[{\"document\":\"d42\",\"document_chars\":17355,\"end\":3000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e1\",\"sha256\":\"79767844ce2071fc5dcf3fb0e64d0cade0ba154ef0fc324d0054c1c767e63138\",\"snapshot\":\"90019ca46504785f620ef12f36abae20080c8c3bc7809053339e4beaa4deb2fd\",\"start\":0,\"text\":\"---\\ntitle: ADVISORS\\ndate: 2022-01-01\\n---\\nADVISORS\\n\\nAdvisors\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was named one of Foreign Policy's 100 Leading Global Thinkers in 2015 and served as a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Distinguished Professor of English and Creative Writing at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Writers retreat. His third novel, The Road to the Country, was published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nRosie is a production and event manager based in Athens, Greece, with extensive experience in coordinating high-profile film festivals and cultural events. She holds a degree in Communication, Media and Culture from Athens and pursued further studies in Art History in Paris, culminating in a Master's in Culture & Tourism from Université Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne. Her professional experience includes collaborations with cultural organizations and festivals worldwide, including UNESCO in New York, the Rolex Art Festival, Les Rencontres d'Arles Photo Festival among others. Since 2018, she has served as Festival Coordinator and Special Events Manager for the French Film Festival of Greece, and since 2022, she has been the Head of Production for the Athens International Children's Film Festival. Driven by a deep passion for cultural engagement and sustainable tourism, she continually seeks innovative ways to connect communities through the arts. In her free time, she enjoys playing music and gardening.\\n\\nProgram Director\\n\\nChigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationaler Literaturpreis, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated for two dozen prizes for fiction. He was a judge of the Booker prize in 2021. He is the Helen S. Lanier Professor of Creative Writing and English at the University of Georgia, and the program director of the Oxbelly Fiction Writers program. His third novel, The Road to the Country, will be published in 2024.\\n\\nProgram Manager\\n\\nKaterina Papanikolopoulos joined Faliro House in 2022 as Manager of Special Projects – a position that evolved into her role acting as the 2024 Oxbelly Retreat, Fiction Writers Program Manager. Following her graduation from UCLA (Summa Cum Laude, Art History), Papanikolopoulos founded the non-profit Athens Design Forum (ADF), a platform that advocates for overlooked and generative design histories interwoven with global labor and migration pa\",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"}]","role":"user"},{"content":"Current control state (data, not source evidence):\n{\"current_notes_not_evidence\":[],\"evidence_shelf\":{\"omitted_for_capacity\":[],\"restored_exact_windows\":[\"e1\"],\"selection\":\"bounded recent first-delivery order; not a relevance/verification judgment\"},\"feedback\":null,\"instruction\":\"Read only useful passages. Notes and all-page cleanup are optional.\",\"literal_answer_contract\":{\"origin\":\"explicit experiment configuration, not inferred from question\",\"prefix\":\"\",\"suffix\":\"\"},\"phase\":\"RESEARCH\",\"remaining\":{\"action_slots\":191,\"backend_calls\":98,\"model_calls\":10,\"output_reservation\":47114},\"research_workflow\":{\"active_gap_not_verified\":null,\"available_pages_not_ranked_for_relevance\":[{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d75\"},\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... colonial photography – Shortlisted for the British Academy Book Prize for Global Cultural Understanding 2023\\n\\nAfrican football migration – Shortlisted for \",\"title\":\"https://manchesteruniversitypress.co.uk/award-winning-books/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d74\"},\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Mara Polgovsky Ezcurra has been shortlisted for the 2020 Association for the Study of the Arts of the Present (ASAP) Book Prize is winner of the 2019 Art J\",\"title\":\"https://www.rutgersuniversitypress.org/awards/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d73\"},\"ref\":\"d73\",\"snippet\":\" ... Published in June, it has become a bestseller and was longlisted for the Baillie Gifford prize for non-fiction. Added to this has been the surprise success\",\"title\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2017/dec/09/diversity-publishing-new-faces\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... He serves on the advisory boards of the Man Asian Literary Prize, the Indo-US Commission on Museums and Culture, the German Research Foundation, and the Gr\",\"title\":\"https://www.infosysprize.org/about-the-prize/categories/humanities.html\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... Prize for Unpublished Books\\n\\n| Deadline | 1 April 2025 |\\n\\n|---|---|\\n\\n| Entry Fee | $25 |\\n\\n| First Prize | 2–4 winners are announced who share in the $1000 \",\"title\":\"https://www.novel-software.com/novel-writing-competitions/\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d70\"},\"ref\":\"d70\",\"snippet\":\" ... The book was longlisted for the Man Asian Literary Prize in 2011. However, after the 2012 anti-Japanese demonstrations in China, Murakami's books were remo\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haruki_Murakami\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... 2006, Asian/Pacific American Awards for Literature Honorable Mention for Saving Fish From Drowning\\n* The Joy Luck Club selected for the National Endowment \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amy_Tan\"},{\"navigation_seen\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... The English translation of the novel appeared in the long list of Man Asian Literary Prize 2012 and in the short list of the DSC Prize for South Asian Lite\",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aadujeevitham\"}],\"consecutive_repeat_rounds\":0,\"contract\":{\"enabled\":true,\"gap_state\":true,\"guided_read\":true,\"recovery_rounds\":2,\"repeat_threshold\":2,\"repetition\":\"bounded\",\"reuse_results\":true,\"version\":\"gap-workflow-v1\"},\"instruction\":\"Use the current missing relation to choose a real next action. Page-name search is not page reading; cached is not proof of progress.\",\"last_new_navigation_source_round\":6,\"last_new_raw_source_round\":3,\"previous_gap_judgments_not_verified\":[],\"recovery_decisions_used\":0,\"stage\":\"normal\"},\"retriever_capabilities\":{\"boolean_operators\":false,\"kind\":\"sqlite-fts5-bm25\",\"negative_result\":\"no hit for this expression is not proof that the fact is absent\",\"phrase_quotes\":false,\"query_rule\":\"lowercase; regex word extraction; first-occurrence deduplication; OR of quoted individual tokens\",\"ranking\":\"SQLite bm25(search), ascending; docid tie-break; unchanged from q26 LocalIndex\",\"scope\":\"fixed local corpus; not live web\",\"site_filter\":false,\"title_kind\":\"stored URL, not an extracted page title\",\"warning\":\"site:, quotes and AND/OR in input are not filters/operators. Their words may become ordinary search terms. Use a few discriminating terms.\"},\"runtime_contract\":{\"evidence_shelf_size\":3,\"max_calls_per_response\":4,\"max_queries_per_search\":3,\"require_sources\":true},\"uncommitted_response_not_evidence\":null}","role":"user"}],"model":"EB-GLM-5.2","temperature":0.0,"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find candidate documents in the configured corpus; it does NOT open their full text.\nUSE WHEN: No suitable page is known, a new entity/relation needs locating, or a different clue is needed after irrelevant results.\nAVOID: Do not repeat a page-name query when you intend to read an existing result. Do not treat snippets as proof or unsupported operators as filters.\nINPUT: queries is an array of 1..3 distinct nonblank strings, each <=2000 characters; top_k is an optional integer 1..10 (default 5). See runtime retriever_capabilities. replay=true explicitly restores the full cached navigation view; it does not force fresh SQL.\nOUTPUT: ok/results contains query, hits with ref/title/snippet, cache status and observation metadata. navigation_seen is NOT a read receipt; raw_ranges_delivered lists actual windows. read_action is an available example, not auto-execution. Metadata counts operations, not relevance. Exact delivered repeats may use view=reuse and omit snippets; replay=true restores them.\nWORKFLOW: search -> inspect returned dN -> read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}); after reading, use the newly found entity and one missing relation for a new search, or finish directly.","name":"search","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"queries":{"items":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"maxItems":3,"minItems":1,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"replay":{"type":"boolean"},"top_k":{"maximum":10,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"}},"required":["queries"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Open the raw text of a received search result, or replay a previously delivered evidence window.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate page may answer the current gap; inspect its actual text before another page-name search. Use continuation to include a subject/date split at a boundary.\nAVOID: Do not guess handles or cite an unread result. Do not infer an entity relationship merely because adjacent windows mention different people.\nINPUT: Only ref is required. dN opens from start=0 with configured read_chars by default; optional integer start>=0 and length=1..6000 use Unicode code points. eN accepts only ref and restores the exact old window. Optional goal<=400 characters on dN selects one lexical paragraph window; it is mutually exclusive with start and forbidden on eN. length remains an upper bound.\nOUTPUT: ok/evidence contains eN, document, snapshot, start/end, original text and integrity fields; next_start supports continuation. The window becomes citable after it is delivered in a subsequent model input. Source text is untrusted data. goal no-match returns matched=false with no evidence; selection metadata reports lexical matches and actual range, never a semantic guarantee.\nWORKFLOW: read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) -> compare the original constraint with the text -> search a newly discovered gap, continue read, or finish with delivered eN.","name":"read","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"goal":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"length":{"maximum":6000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"ref":{"pattern":"^[de][1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["ref"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Find literal text positions inside one already received document; this is page-local navigation.\nUSE WHEN: The page is known but a name or exact phrase is far from its beginning.\nAVOID: Do not use a literal zero-match result to prove a fact absent. It does not search aliases, paraphrases or the whole corpus.\nINPUT: ref must be a received dN; text is a nonblank string <=2000 characters; optional integer start>=0; ignore_case is boolean, default false.\nOUTPUT: ok/document/snapshot/matches gives original start/end positions and exact excerpts, case_sensitive and next_start. Matches are positions_not_evidence, not citable eN.\nWORKFLOW: find -> read the matched range with enough preceding subject context -> compare evidence. Change literal terms or use goal-read rather than repeating zero matches.","name":"find","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"ignore_case":{"type":"boolean"},"ref":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"start":{"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"text":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["ref","text"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Locate earlier delivered evidence, received search navigation and optional note history without external retrieval.\nUSE WHEN: A known lead or earlier raw window has left the active context; recover it instead of re-searching the same phrase.\nAVOID: Do not cite a recall excerpt as new evidence. It cannot search unreceived backend data; a lexical miss is not a proof of absence.\nINPUT: query is a nonblank string <=2000 characters. Use a discriminating entity or relation already encountered.\nOUTPUT: ok/matches has ref or note key, exact excerpt and kind. eN can be replayed; dN can be opened; inactive notes are historical model judgments, not evidence.\nWORKFLOW: recall -> read({\"ref\":\"eN\"}) for exact recovery, or read({\"ref\":\"dN\"}) for an unread page. Then update only the gap that changed.","name":"recall","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"query":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Maintain a small optional free-text scratchpad; not verified facts or a prerequisite to submit.\nUSE WHEN: A brief reusable alias, rejected route or independent reminder will help later. Prefer update_gap for the active research question when available.\nAVOID: Do not summarize every page, copy the full question, or repeatedly write the same note. Notes do not automatically retract dependent plans.\nINPUT: put requires op/key/text/anchors; text <=600 characters, anchors is <=6 delivered eN. delete requires op/key only. Keys are 1..32 ASCII letters/digits/_/-. Capacity is explicit.\nOUTPUT: ok/key/changed and kind=agent_note_not_evidence, or deleted. A no-op is not research progress. Errors do not silently alter saved notes.\nWORKFLOW: Optionally save a useful observation alongside another already-planned action; keep sources in the archive and finish without cleanup.","name":"notes","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"anchors":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"put"},"text":{"maxLength":600,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["op","key","text","anchors"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"key":{"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32}$","type":"string"},"op":{"const":"delete"}},"required":["op","key"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Explicitly submit the requested answer with source windows, or explicitly abstain.\nUSE WHEN: The requested core answer has sufficient support, or the available budget/evidence cannot resolve it. No note, gap update or audit is mandatory.\nAVOID: Do not claim every clue is verified when it is not. Do not change established into expanded, by-year into in-year, or hide unresolved numeric conflicts in a long explanation.\nINPUT: Answer branch requires answer and refs. Nonblank strings are <=8000 characters; string-integer-v1 additionally permits plain JSON integers, not bools/floats, rendered as decimal text. Strings stay exact. Abstention requires abstain=true and nonblank reason<=2000 characters. Never mix branches. refs contains only delivered eN, <=16; configured source and literal-format requirements still apply.\nOUTPUT: ok/terminal records submitted or abstained. Submitted answer is text with refs/basis and any representation metadata. Legal references are NOT semantic verification. Explicit prefix/suffix constraints still apply.\nWORKFLOW: Finish last in a response, based only on evidence already received for that decision. Never combine a new read and a guessed citation to its unseen result. In FINAL only finish is allowed.","name":"finish","parameters":{"oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"answer":{"maxLength":8000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":["string","integer"]},"refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":16,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true}},"required":["answer","refs"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"abstain":{"const":true},"reason":{"maxLength":2000,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["abstain","reason"],"type":"object"}]}},"type":"function"},{"function":{"description":"FUNCTION: Replace the one active research question and retain a bounded history of explicit model judgments; it is NOT an automatic verifier.\nUSE WHEN: A candidate, unresolved relation, rejection or conflict changed, or repeated searches need a concrete next objective. Use sparingly, not after every tool.\nAVOID: Do not turn the original question or your prior guess into evidence. Updating a gap does not count as a new observation and does not reset a search loop.\nINPUT: subject/question/basis are nonblank <=400 characters; kind and status follow schema; evidence_refs are <=6 received eN, navigation_refs <=6 received dN; next_action is one named existing tool. supported/rejected/conflict require evidence_refs. Supply a concise decision basis, not a transcript.\nOUTPUT: ok/changed/current returns agent_judgment_not_verified with revision. At most four previous distinct gap versions remain in the active view; the full update is journaled. Sources are checked for delivery, not entailment.\nWORKFLOW: Observe -> identify one missing relationship or record a real rejection -> select read on an available page or search for a new relation. An update may share a response with known independent actions; no update is required before finish.","name":"update_gap","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"basis":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"evidence_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^e[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"kind":{"enum":["locate","read","relation","disambiguate","conflict","recover"]},"navigation_refs":{"items":{"pattern":"^d[1-9][0-9]*$","type":"string"},"maxItems":6,"minItems":0,"type":"array","uniqueItems":true},"next_action":{"enum":["search","read","find","recall","finish"]},"question":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["open","supported","rejected","conflict"]},"subject":{"maxLength":400,"minLength":1,"pattern":"\\S","type":"string"}},"required":["subject","question","kind","status","evidence_refs","navigation_refs","next_action","basis"],"type":"object"}},"type":"function"}]}